  "body": {
    "id": "thm:honest-root-n-confidence",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For a suitable choice of the simultaneous-concentration constant in \\(r_{n,\\alpha}\\), both the original summary-inversion set and the computable outer set are honest:\n\\[\n\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M}Q_P^{(n)}\\{\n\\nu_P\\in\\mathcal C_{n,\\alpha}\\cap\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{alg}}_{n,\\alpha}\\}\n\\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nBoth sets are nonempty on every sample, and\n\\[\n\\operatorname{diam}_{W_1}(\\mathcal C_{n,\\alpha})\n\\le4C_{\\mathrm{mod}}r_{n,\\alpha},\n\\qquad\n\\operatorname{diam}_{W_1}(\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{alg}}_{n,\\alpha})\n\\le2R_{n,\\alpha}.\n\\]\nThe second set has the explicit fixed-dimensional constrained-program representation in \\(\\mathrm{def:wasserstein\\text{-}confidence\\text{-}set}\\).  Coverage and root-\\(n\\) \\(W_1\\)-diameter are uniform over every collision, merge, and split stratum; neither equality nor inclusion between the two confidence sets is claimed.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(C_{\\mathrm{mod}}\\)",
      "\\(r_{n,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M\\)",
      "\\(Q_P^{(n)}\\)",
      "\\(\\nu_P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal C_{n,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{alg}}_{n,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(R_{n,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(W_1\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:bounded-x",
      "ass:bounded-proxy-product",
      "ass:bounded-outcome-proxy-product",
      "ass:latent-arm-positivity",
      "def:model-class",
      "def:sample-experiment",
      "def:wasserstein-confidence-set",
      "prop:summary-repair-total-borel",
      "prop:polynomial-net-law-estimator",
